# Copy to backend/.env for `make dev-backend`; it is never committed. Production sets the same names
# in its environment. A double underscore is a section: Api__CorsOrigins__0 is Api:CorsOrigins:0.

# Development turns on the API reference at /scalar and readable logs (make dev-backend's default).
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development

# Host headers the API answers to, separated by ';' (api.example.com). * accepts any.
AllowedHosts=*

# Browser origins allowed to call the API directly (CORS), one per index. Behind the Next.js proxy
# none are needed.
# Api__CorsOrigins__0=https://app.example.com

# Limits, with their defaults.
# Api__MaxRequestBodyBytes=1048576
# Api__RequestTimeoutSeconds=30
# Api__RateLimitPerMinute=600

# OpenTelemetry: nothing is exported until an endpoint is set (the Aspire dashboard locally, any OTLP
# collector in production). The service name defaults to appsettings.json's OpenTelemetry:ServiceName.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4317
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=

# The database: one Postgres for every module (each keeps its tables in its own schema). `make
# migrate` creates them; `make seed` adds example data. Unset, /health/ready answers 503.
# Quote it: make sources this file, and the shell would split the value at each semicolon.
# ConnectionStrings__Default="Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=app;Username=postgres;Password=postgres"

# The cache: HybridCache keeps entries in each instance's memory. Set a Valkey (or Redis) connection string to
# share them between instances; unset, each instance has its own and that is fine. A removal clears the shared
# entry, but other instances keep their in-memory copy until Cache__LocalExpirationMinutes pass.
# ConnectionStrings__Cache=localhost:6379
# Cache__ExpirationMinutes=5
# Cache__LocalExpirationMinutes=1
# Cache__MaximumPayloadBytes=1048576
# Cache__SharedTimeoutMilliseconds=100
# Cache__KeyPrefix=app:
# Feature flags, in Microsoft's schema. appsettings.json defines notes-list; override one in the environment
# (a flag that is not defined is off). Flags:Public lists the flags GET /v1/flags may show a signed-in user.
# feature_management__feature_flags__0__id=notes-list
# feature_management__feature_flags__0__enabled=false
# Flags__Public__0=notes-list

# Sign-in: the issuer of the access tokens the API accepts. Unset, every protected endpoint answers
# 401. The local Keycloak (backend/keycloak) serves plain HTTP, so it turns the HTTPS check off.
# Auth__Issuer=http://localhost:8080/realms/app
# Auth__RequireHttpsMetadata=false
# When the API reaches the issuer at another address than the one tokens name (in Compose, say):
# Auth__MetadataAddress=http://keycloak:8080/realms/app/.well-known/openid-configuration
# Auth__Audience=api
